---
const pillars = [
  {
    title: "Technical",
    body: "Understanding how modern AI systems work, where they fail, and what makes them difficult to align, interpret, and evaluate.",
  },
  {
    title: "Policy & Governance",
    body: "Examining the institutions, regulations, and international frameworks needed to manage the deployment of increasingly capable systems.",
  },
  {
    title: "Philosophy & Ethics",
    body: "Asking what 'safe' and 'aligned' actually mean — questions of value, uncertainty, and responsibility that technical work alone cannot answer.",
  },
];
---

<section id="approach" class="scroll-mt-24 border-b border-slate-200">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
    <h2 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
      Our Approach
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      AI risk isn't purely a technical problem or a policy problem: it spans
      computer science, public policy, philosophy and ethics, economics, and
      law. We think that's a strength, not a complication.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {
        pillars.map((pillar) => (
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">{pillar.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
              {pillar.body}
            </p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">+ More</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
          We are growing to include economics, law, and other disciplines. If
          you think that your field belongs in this conversation, then it
          probably does.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
